                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "You slept eight hours and people still ask if you\u0027re tired. Concealer helps till lunch, and the eye cream on your shelf hasn\u0027t done much. Thing is, dark circles come in a few different kinds, and our dark circles treatment in Delhi begins by figuring out which kind is yours.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "2. What Are Dark Circles?",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "They\u0027re the darker or shadowy patches under your eyes that make you look worn out, even on a good day. For some people the colour is actual pigment sitting in the skin. For others, the skin there is so thin that the veins underneath show through as a bluish or purplish tinge. And sometimes there\u0027s a small hollow under the eye that simply catches shadow. Plenty of people have two or all three going on. They don\u0027t usually fade on their own, and with age they often get a little deeper.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "So the first visit is mostly about looking closely. The dermatologist checks how thick your under-eye skin is, how deep any pigment goes, whether you\u0027ve lost some fat in that area, and how visible the blood vessels are. Once that\u0027s clear, your dark circles can be put into a type: pigmented, volume-related, vascular, or mixed. The type is what decides the treatment.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "3. Causes of Dark Circles",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Ageing skin:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " the under-eye skin gets thinner and loses support, so veins show through more",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Losing volume:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " less fat under the eyes leaves a hollow, and hollows throw shadows",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Pigment:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " extra melanin collects in the area, and for many people this simply runs in the family",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Sun:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " years without sunscreen darken and weaken skin that\u0027s already delicate",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Sleep and stress:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " irregular nights and a stressful routine show up first around the eyes",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Screens:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " long hours staring at a phone or laptop strain the eyes and can make circles stand out more",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Not drinking enough water:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " dehydrated skin looks duller and hollows look deeper",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "City air:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " pollution keeps the skin mildly irritated, and in Delhi that\u0027s hard to avoid",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "4. Prevention Tips",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Put sunscreen under your eyes too:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " most people stop at the cheeks, so pick a gentle one and take it all the way up",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Try to sleep at the same time each night:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " consistency matters more than the odd long lie-in",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Drink water through the day:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " well-hydrated skin hides shadows better",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Give your eyes screen breaks:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " every so often, look away and rest them for a minute",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Stop rubbing:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " it irritates the thin skin and can make pigment worse",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Keep under-eye skincare simple:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " strong actives meant for the face can sting and inflame this area, so ask your dermatologist what to use",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "See a doctor if nothing\u0027s changing:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " a quick check tells you whether it\u0027s pigment, hollowness or veins, which beats months of trying random creams",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "5. Treatments for Dark Circles at Dadu Medical Centre\u0027s Clinic, Delhi",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "li",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Laser Toning:",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " slowly lightens under-eye pigment so the area looks brighter and more even",
                         "b":  false
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  ". ",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
