    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "6. Why Choose Dr. Nivedita Dadu",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Most people who come to us with dark circles have already spent a fair bit on creams that didn\u0027t work, usually because the real cause was never looked at. At Dr. Nivedita Dadu\u0027s clinics in Vasant Vihar and Rajouri Garden, we start with your under-eyes, not a product. Once we know whether it\u0027s pigment, hollowness, visible veins or a mix, the plan is built around that. Treatments are done under a doctor\u0027s supervision with settings suited to sensitive and Indian skin, and we keep checking in so the plan can shift if your skin responds differently than expected.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "h2",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "7. FAQs",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Will my dark circles go away for good?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Results can last a long while, but most people need the odd top-up. Your skin keeps ageing and life keeps happening, and both show under the eyes.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: How do I know which treatment suits me?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. You don\u0027t have to guess. The dermatologist looks at whether it\u0027s pigment, a hollow, visible veins or a combination, and suggests treatment from there.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Isn\u0027t it just pigmentation?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Often not. Thin skin showing the veins underneath, or a small hollow casting shadow, is just as common, and those need a different approach.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: My skin is sensitive. Is this safe?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Yes, as long as it\u0027s done under medical supervision with settings chosen for your skin.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: How long before I see a difference?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. That depends on the cause and the treatment. Some people notice brighter skin first, others smoother texture or softer hollows. It tends to build slowly.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Can an eye cream fix this?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. Usually not on its own. A good cream can support treatment, but for most people it won\u0027t solve the problem.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Do screens make dark circles worse?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. They can. Long screen hours strain the eyes and make existing circles look more obvious.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: Do men get this treated too?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. All the time. A lot of our dark circle patients are men.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
    {
        "k":  "p",
        "runs":  [
                     {
                         "t":  "Q: How much does treatment cost in Delhi?",
                         "b":  true
                     },
                     {
                         "t":  " \nAns. It varies with the cause, the treatment and how many sessions you need. We\u0027ll give you the figure after your consultation.",
                         "b":  false
                     }
                 ]
    },
